22
00:03:21.241 --> 00:03:33.153
<v Maya>Yeah. The AI required immense hand-holding, constant correction, and just total micromanagement from a human expert. Left to its own devices, it couldn't just autonomously walk through the problem.</v>

23
00:03:33.553 --> 00:03:48.418
<v Daniel>Which led Schwartz to his core realization today. Looking back at that slog, he identified what physicists call an impedance mismatch. I love this concept, but I want to make sure I'm visualizing it right. It's essentially an engineering term,</v>

